    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d123">

                <pb facs="0412" n="364" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg364"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram per cable.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Johnson</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 24, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Insist on convention like 1853, without now naming arbiter. Convention must be
                    submitted to Senate and the country. Objection would be raised to any arbiter
                    who could be named in advance. When convention goes into effect, the two
                    governments can instruct the commissioners to agree on arbiter.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reverdy Johnson,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
